  "id": "COMPOUND:3295 - PROTEIN:4590",
  "verbalization": "Flavopiridol is implicated in the regulation of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 5 (MRP5) through a complex network of targets. The evidence suggests that flavopiridol acts as a target of two distinct compounds, Sinocalycanchinensin G, which in turn targets MRP5. This indicates a potential pathway where flavopiridol may influence MRP5 activity via the intermediacy of Sinocalycanchinensin G. The presence of two separate but overlapping targets for Sinocalycanchinensin G implies that the compound may exert its effects through multiple mechanisms, possibly involving different downstream pathways. The integration of these findings highlights the role of Sinocalycanchinensin G as a critical mediator in the interaction between flavopiridol and MRP5, suggesting a possible regulatory or inhibitory relationship that could be relevant in therapeutic contexts.",
